  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_cow_et_calf_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>meaning unknown (Cobb 10 n. 2 defines this term as 'arrow-root': 'a nutritious starch prepared by crushing the corns of the arum maculatum, which is native to Britain. Here however, the product is shipped in maundes, baskets and dozens, which would seem to exclude its definition as a starch) | meaning unknown (Cobb 174 records 'arrow-root', but this is not recorded in OED s.v. arrow-root and is very unlikely, since kow et calffe is shipped here in dozens) | meaning unknown | meaning unknown (Cobb 174 records 'arrow-root', but this is not recorded in OED s.v. arrow-root)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
